Task: Implement (Green) - DELETE /orders/{id} endpoint

Summary:
Added OrderStore[F].delete(id): F[Boolean] to both backends. In-memory:
Ref.modify, removing the key if present and returning whether it existed.
Postgres: DELETE ... RETURNING id via .option, so deleted = result.isDefined -
mirrors the RETURNING + .option pattern already used for get/update, avoiding
a separate Command/Completion API.

Added a tapir DELETE /orders/{id} endpoint - 204 No Content on success, the
existing notFoundOutput (404) if the id doesn't exist. Wired into
OrderRoutes.routes and Main's Docs.routes list.

Extended OrderRoutesSuite (204 + subsequent GET 404, 404-for-unknown-id, and
logging tests for DELETE; failingStore now implements delete) and
OrderStorePostgresSuite (delete success/unknown-id/malformed-id tests against
real Postgres).

